1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:01,410
If your knee replacement

2
00:00:01,410 --> 00:00:02,710
still hurts and the X-ray

3
00:00:02,710 --> 00:00:04,250
keeps coming back fine,

4
00:00:04,250 --> 00:00:05,500
don't accept that.

5
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:06,280
I've been a massage

6
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:08,070
therapist for thirty years.

7
00:00:08,070 --> 00:00:09,390
On my feet all day,

8
00:00:09,390 --> 00:00:10,820
leaning over the table,

9
00:00:10,820 --> 00:00:12,710
working on other
people's pain.

10
00:00:12,710 --> 00:00:13,500
I had my right

11
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:15,290
knee replaced
two years ago.

12
00:00:15,290 --> 00:00:17,470
It has hurt every day since.

13
00:00:17,470 --> 00:00:18,990
Not surgery pain.

14
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:20,100
I know what that felt like,

15
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:21,240
and it went away.

16
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:22,370
This is different.

17
00:00:22,370 --> 00:00:23,140
Tight.

18
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:23,980
Full.

19
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:24,820
Like a band around

20
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:26,890
the joint that never loosens.

21
00:00:26,890 --> 00:00:27,860
And for two years

22
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:29,710
I've been told
the same thing.

23
00:00:30,110 --> 00:00:31,110
Give it time.

24
00:00:31,110 --> 00:00:32,850
At six weeks it was swelling,

25
00:00:32,850 --> 00:00:34,630
and swelling is normal.

26
00:00:34,630 --> 00:00:35,610
At three months,

27
00:00:35,610 --> 00:00:36,580
give it six.

28
00:00:36,580 --> 00:00:37,570
At six months,

29
00:00:37,570 --> 00:00:39,620
some knees take a full year.

30
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:40,410
At a year,

31
00:00:40,410 --> 00:00:42,640
eighteen months
isn't unusual.

32
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:44,220
And I didn't just wait.

33
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:46,450
We went down the list.

34
00:00:46,450 --> 00:00:48,090
More physical therapy.

35
00:00:48,090 --> 00:00:51,020
Every session, every
exercise at home.

36
00:00:51,020 --> 00:00:52,330
I got stronger.

37
00:00:52,330 --> 00:00:54,110
The tightness never moved.

38
00:00:54,110 --> 00:00:55,590
The pain pills helped,

39
00:00:55,590 --> 00:00:57,250
and that was the problem.

40
00:00:57,250 --> 00:00:58,880
I'm already on enough
every morning,

41
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:00,070
and nobody could tell me

42
00:01:00,070 --> 00:01:01,670
when I'd get to stop.

43
00:01:01,670 --> 00:01:02,980
Then a nerve block.

44
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:04,860
Then talk of
burning the nerve.

45
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:05,960
And after that,

46
00:01:05,960 --> 00:01:07,420
a second operation to go

47
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:09,290
back in and do it over.

48
00:01:09,290 --> 00:01:10,410
I said no.

49
00:01:10,410 --> 00:01:11,880
Every morning I stepped out

50
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:13,000
of bed and my knee

51
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:13,890
felt like a band

52
00:01:13,890 --> 00:01:15,360
was wrapped around it,

53
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:18,210
tightening every inch
I tried to straighten.

54
00:01:18,590 --> 00:01:19,950
Every morning I took

55
00:01:19,950 --> 00:01:21,450
something for it and went

56
00:01:21,450 --> 00:01:22,740
to my first client.

57
00:01:22,740 --> 00:01:24,240
Couldn't do the stairs,

58
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:25,370
couldn't get through an hour

59
00:01:25,370 --> 00:01:27,010
at the table without a break,

60
00:01:27,010 --> 00:01:28,230
couldn't stand at the counter

61
00:01:28,230 --> 00:01:30,150
long enough to finish dinner,

62
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:32,130
couldn't sit through
my granddaughter's

63
00:01:32,130 --> 00:01:35,070
game without shifting
every two minutes.

64
00:01:35,070 --> 00:01:36,590
It woke me at night,

65
00:01:36,590 --> 00:01:39,110
and it turned
ordinary things,

66
00:01:39,460 --> 00:01:41,020
like getting in the car

67
00:01:41,020 --> 00:01:42,970
or up off the couch,

68
00:01:42,970 --> 00:01:44,210
into a decision.

69
00:01:44,210 --> 00:01:45,720
I started wondering how

70
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:46,750
many more years I had

71
00:01:46,750 --> 00:01:48,150
left at that table.

72
00:01:48,150 --> 00:01:49,650
After a long and serious

73
00:01:49,650 --> 00:01:51,010
talk with my husband,

74
00:01:51,010 --> 00:01:53,360
I went back in
one more time.

75
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:54,540
That was the fourth set

76
00:01:54,540 --> 00:01:56,400
of X-rays on this knee.

77
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:58,050
And like the three before it,

78
00:01:58,050 --> 00:02:00,760
the answer was
everything looks great.

79
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:02,980
No loosening, no infection,

80
00:02:02,980 --> 00:02:04,070
nothing wrong.

81
00:02:04,070 --> 00:02:05,380
Only this time there

82
00:02:05,380 --> 00:02:07,070
was no new number.

83
00:02:07,070 --> 00:02:09,950
Nobody said give it
another six months.

84
00:02:09,950 --> 00:02:11,840
There was nothing
left to give it.

85
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:12,790
I sat in the parking

86
00:02:12,790 --> 00:02:14,230
lot for a while.

87
00:02:14,230 --> 00:02:15,740
Okay, I thought.

88
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:17,490
Then explain this.

89
00:02:17,490 --> 00:02:19,850
Anyway, a couple
of months back,

90
00:02:19,850 --> 00:02:21,460
I hit my breaking point.

91
00:02:21,460 --> 00:02:23,590
It was around 2:30
in the morning.

92
00:02:23,590 --> 00:02:24,410
I had a full day

93
00:02:24,410 --> 00:02:26,370
of clients starting at nine.

94
00:02:26,370 --> 00:02:27,230
Everyone in the house

95
00:02:27,230 --> 00:02:29,230
was asleep and I
was downstairs

96
00:02:29,230 --> 00:02:31,060
in the recliner
with my leg up,

97
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:32,070
trying to find any

98
00:02:32,070 --> 00:02:33,270
angle where it didn't

99
00:02:33,270 --> 00:02:34,400
feel like something
was wrapped

100
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:36,150
around my knee
and tightening.

101
00:02:36,150 --> 00:02:38,680
My husband didn't know
I'd come downstairs.

102
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:40,910
By then I'd stopped
telling him.

103
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:41,850
And I just thought,

104
00:02:41,850 --> 00:02:43,510
is this really my life now?

105
00:02:43,510 --> 00:02:45,010
I can't live like this.

106
00:02:45,010 --> 00:02:46,790
So I made myself a promise.

107
00:02:46,790 --> 00:02:47,600
I wouldn't go a day

108
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:49,300
without looking
for an answer.

109
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:50,560
And when I found one,

110
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:51,600
I'd share it with everyone

111
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:53,330
going through
the same thing.

112
00:02:53,330 --> 00:02:54,250
So I got my laptop

113
00:02:54,250 --> 00:02:55,720
out and went looking.

114
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:57,160
Not for a product.

115
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:58,510
For an explanation.

116
00:02:58,510 --> 00:03:00,060
Mayo Clinic forums,

117
00:03:00,060 --> 00:03:02,150
the knee replacement
group on Facebook,

118
00:03:02,150 --> 00:03:05,020
doctor videos,
medical animations.

119
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:06,010
And that's when I found

120
00:03:06,010 --> 00:03:07,160
a video from a physical

121
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:08,680
therapist named Dr.

122
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:10,820
Steven Salinger,
whose own wife

123
00:03:10,820 --> 00:03:13,010
had been through
exactly this.

124
00:03:13,010 --> 00:03:14,850
But before I say
anything else,

125
00:03:14,850 --> 00:03:16,650
I want to be
straight with you.

126
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:19,380
You've already had
something work fast.

127
00:03:19,380 --> 00:03:20,350
The ice.

128
00:03:20,350 --> 00:03:22,100
The first week of a new pill.

129
00:03:22,100 --> 00:03:23,990
The good day
after a session.

130
00:03:23,990 --> 00:03:25,520
Then it wore off.

131
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:27,880
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

132
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:29,900
Fast relief isn't relief.

133
00:03:29,900 --> 00:03:31,250
It's a preview.

134
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:32,890
So I'm not going

135
00:03:32,890 --> 00:03:34,630
to tell you this works fast.

136
00:03:34,630 --> 00:03:35,800
It doesn't.

137
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:37,670
But if you're willing
to be patient,

138
00:03:37,670 --> 00:03:38,550
and to look at what's

139
00:03:38,550 --> 00:03:39,670
going on around your new

140
00:03:39,670 --> 00:03:41,740
knee instead of inside it,

141
00:03:41,740 --> 00:03:42,560
there is a real

142
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:44,460
reason it still hurts.

143
00:03:44,460 --> 00:03:46,380
And something you
can do about it.

144
00:03:46,380 --> 00:03:48,080
Let me explain what he said,

145
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:48,890
because this is what

146
00:03:48,890 --> 00:03:50,530
changed everything for me.

147
00:03:50,530 --> 00:03:52,420
He started with the basics.

148
00:03:52,420 --> 00:03:53,620
A knee replacement takes

149
00:03:53,620 --> 00:03:55,360
out the worn joint surfaces

150
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:57,410
and puts in metal
and plastic.

151
00:03:57,410 --> 00:03:58,920
That's what stops
the arthritis

152
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:01,180
pain you had before
the operation.

153
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:03,660
That part I already knew.

154
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:05,470
But then he
explained something

155
00:04:05,470 --> 00:04:07,140
nobody had ever told me.

156
00:04:07,140 --> 00:04:08,440
He said, think about

157
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:10,530
a swollen foot inside a shoe.

158
00:04:10,530 --> 00:04:11,890
The shoe didn't shrink.

159
00:04:11,890 --> 00:04:14,000
Your foot is taking
up more room,

160
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:15,390
so everything feels cramped

161
00:04:15,390 --> 00:04:17,220
and tight and squeezed.

162
00:04:17,220 --> 00:04:18,260
Your new knee sits

163
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:20,130
in a limited space with living

164
00:04:20,130 --> 00:04:21,800
tissue packed all around it.

165
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:22,970
To put that knee in,

166
00:04:22,970 --> 00:04:23,620
the surgeon had

167
00:04:23,620 --> 00:04:25,120
to work through that tissue.

168
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:27,700
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

169
00:04:27,700 --> 00:04:29,480
At first that's normal.

170
00:04:29,910 --> 00:04:31,080
But in some people

171
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:32,400
that swelling can
stay switched

172
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:34,580
on far longer than expected.

173
00:04:34,580 --> 00:04:35,960
And swollen tissue takes up

174
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:38,070
more room than
calm tissue does.

175
00:04:38,070 --> 00:04:39,320
So when you bend,

176
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:41,400
that tissue gets compressed.

177
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:42,690
When you straighten,

178
00:04:42,690 --> 00:04:44,120
it gets pulled tight.

179
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,170
That's the band.

180
00:04:45,170 --> 00:04:47,590
That's the ache that
never quite leaves.

181
00:04:47,590 --> 00:04:48,370
And you start being

182
00:04:48,370 --> 00:04:49,490
the one who says,

183
00:04:49,490 --> 00:04:50,560
you go ahead.

184
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:51,700
I'll stay here.

185
00:04:51,700 --> 00:04:53,220
And that's exactly
why so much

186
00:04:53,220 --> 00:04:55,500
of what I'd tried
hadn't worked.

187
00:04:56,150 --> 00:04:57,670
Physical therapy strengthens

188
00:04:57,670 --> 00:04:59,220
the muscles
around the knee.

189
00:04:59,220 --> 00:05:01,330
Worth doing, and I'd done it.

190
00:05:01,330 --> 00:05:02,290
It does nothing about

191
00:05:02,290 --> 00:05:03,790
tissue taking up room.

192
00:05:03,790 --> 00:05:04,970
A nerve block quiets

193
00:05:04,970 --> 00:05:07,220
the nerve carrying
the signal.

194
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:09,680
It doesn't touch
what's generating it.

195
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:10,800
But when that irritated

196
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:12,360
tissue finally calms down,

197
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:13,800
it holds less fluid,

198
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:15,470
and it takes up less room.

199
00:05:15,470 --> 00:05:16,770
Less room taken up means

200
00:05:16,770 --> 00:05:18,720
less pressure
squeezing the joint.

201
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:20,590
That's what takes
the pressure off.

202
00:05:20,590 --> 00:05:22,210
After two years of this,

203
00:05:22,210 --> 00:05:24,020
it finally made sense.

204
00:05:24,410 --> 00:05:26,400
The problem was
never the new knee.

205
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:28,360
It was the tissue
crowded around it.

206
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:29,970
He calls it the squeeze.

207
00:05:29,970 --> 00:05:31,140
Once you've felt it,

208
00:05:31,140 --> 00:05:32,280
that's the word.

209
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:33,560
I'd bought knee sleeves,

210
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:35,840
compression braces,
a cushioned mat

211
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:37,310
to stand on at the table,

212
00:05:37,310 --> 00:05:39,520
creams, half of
Amazon really,

213
00:05:39,520 --> 00:05:40,410
and all any of it

214
00:05:40,410 --> 00:05:41,800
gave me was an hour.

215
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:42,760
I even looked at going

216
00:05:42,760 --> 00:05:44,750
to a clinic for the
light therapy.

217
00:05:44,750 --> 00:05:46,300
But at $200 a session

218
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:48,090
with nothing covered
by insurance,

219
00:05:48,090 --> 00:05:49,400
that was a quick no.

220
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:50,380
Then one night I went

221
00:05:50,380 --> 00:05:51,540
back to that knee
replacement

222
00:05:51,540 --> 00:05:53,240
group and actually read it.

223
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:54,800
Thousands of people,

224
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:56,660
years out from surgery,

225
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,570
comparing notes on stiffness

226
00:05:58,570 --> 00:06:01,470
and tightness nobody
could explain.

227
00:06:01,470 --> 00:06:03,460
And no matter
how far I scrolled,

228
00:06:03,460 --> 00:06:05,400
the same thing
kept coming up.

229
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:07,070
This one device,

230
00:06:07,070 --> 00:06:08,020
and people saying it

231
00:06:08,020 --> 00:06:08,920
was the first thing

232
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:10,390
that made a difference.

233
00:06:10,770 --> 00:06:13,030
And before anyone
jumps in thinking,

234
00:06:13,030 --> 00:06:14,720
alright, here it comes,

235
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:16,210
she's selling me something,

236
00:06:16,210 --> 00:06:18,090
let me shut that
down right now.

237
00:06:18,090 --> 00:06:19,130
I'm only here because

238
00:06:19,130 --> 00:06:20,470
I made myself a promise

239
00:06:20,470 --> 00:06:22,270
at 2:30 in the morning

240
00:06:22,270 --> 00:06:23,030
that if I ever

241
00:06:23,030 --> 00:06:24,310
found something
that helped,

242
00:06:24,310 --> 00:06:25,560
I'd say so.

243
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:27,200
It's called the KenRelief

244
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:29,100
Red Light Therapy Wrap.

245
00:06:29,760 --> 00:06:32,060
At first glance I didn't buy it.

246
00:06:32,060 --> 00:06:33,120
It looked like the cheap

247
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:34,630
knee sleeves off Amazon

248
00:06:34,630 --> 00:06:36,210
that did nothing for me.

249
00:06:36,210 --> 00:06:38,190
But I went to their
website anyway,

250
00:06:38,190 --> 00:06:38,870
just to see what

251
00:06:38,870 --> 00:06:40,390
all the fuss was about.

252
00:06:40,390 --> 00:06:41,910
It's the same red
light therapy

253
00:06:41,910 --> 00:06:44,750
clinics charge
$200 a session for,

254
00:06:44,750 --> 00:06:47,470
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

255
00:06:47,470 --> 00:06:48,400
in a wrap you plug

256
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:50,280
into the wall at home.

257
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:52,010
Two hundred
and forty lights.

258
00:06:52,010 --> 00:06:54,040
Red at 660 nanometers

259
00:06:54,040 --> 00:06:56,690
and near-infrared at 850,

260
00:06:56,690 --> 00:06:59,030
run together for the
strongest effect.

261
00:06:59,030 --> 00:07:00,490
Four strength levels.

262
00:07:00,490 --> 00:07:02,380
A five to thirty minute timer.

263
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:04,220
Then I saw the guarantee.

264
00:07:04,220 --> 00:07:05,430
Ninety days.

265
00:07:05,430 --> 00:07:07,300
Results or your money back,

266
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:10,160
no questions,
no store credit,

267
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:11,970
and you don't
even send it back.

268
00:07:11,970 --> 00:07:13,790
No physical therapist
ever gave me

269
00:07:13,790 --> 00:07:15,790
ninety days to
change my mind.

270
00:07:15,790 --> 00:07:17,050
There wasn't much to lose,

271
00:07:17,050 --> 00:07:18,290
so I ordered it.

272
00:07:18,290 --> 00:07:18,830
Two of them,

273
00:07:18,830 --> 00:07:19,830
actually.

274
00:07:19,830 --> 00:07:21,340
Only the right
knee was replaced,

275
00:07:21,340 --> 00:07:23,150
but you favor the
leg that hurts,

276
00:07:23,150 --> 00:07:24,890
and I'd done it for two years.

277
00:07:24,890 --> 00:07:26,900
The left one was
carrying the difference.

278
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:27,760
When it came,

279
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:29,730
I strapped it on
expecting nothing,

280
00:07:29,730 --> 00:07:30,680
because I'd been let down

281
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:32,600
too many times
to get excited.

282
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:34,180
What I felt was warmth.

283
00:07:34,820 --> 00:07:36,470
Not a heating
pad kind of hot.

284
00:07:36,470 --> 00:07:37,380
More like it was coming

285
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:38,380
from inside the knee

286
00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:39,640
and spreading around it.

287
00:07:39,640 --> 00:07:40,530
And that was it.

288
00:07:40,530 --> 00:07:42,030
That was the
whole experience.

289
00:07:42,030 --> 00:07:43,160
When I took it off,

290
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:43,880
I'll be honest,

291
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:45,620
nothing dramatic
had happened.

292
00:07:45,620 --> 00:07:47,460
And after what
that video said,

293
00:07:47,460 --> 00:07:49,510
that's exactly
what I expected.

294
00:07:49,510 --> 00:07:50,550
What was different

295
00:07:50,550 --> 00:07:51,460
was that for the first

296
00:07:51,460 --> 00:07:52,550
time in two years

297
00:07:52,550 --> 00:07:54,170
I'd done something
for my knee

298
00:07:54,170 --> 00:07:55,390
instead of to it.

299
00:07:55,390 --> 00:07:57,430
Twenty minutes,
in my own chair.

300
00:07:57,430 --> 00:07:59,180
No drive, no copay.

301
00:07:59,180 --> 00:08:00,590
They say twenty minutes.

302
00:08:00,590 --> 00:08:01,810
I did thirty,

303
00:08:01,810 --> 00:08:02,830
twice a day,

304
00:08:02,830 --> 00:08:04,660
lowest setting
that first week.

305
00:08:04,660 --> 00:08:06,430
Once before my first client,

306
00:08:06,430 --> 00:08:08,210
once after my last.

307
00:08:08,210 --> 00:08:09,280
The first week,

308
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:10,100
I couldn't have told

309
00:08:10,100 --> 00:08:11,940
you if anything
was happening.

310
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:12,550
I tried not

311
00:08:12,550 --> 00:08:13,860
to get my hopes up.

312
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:14,690
I'd had things help

313
00:08:14,690 --> 00:08:16,400
for a week and then stop.

314
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:18,050
But somewhere
in the second

315
00:08:18,050 --> 00:08:19,460
week I noticed
I'd come down

316
00:08:19,460 --> 00:08:21,390
the stairs without
holding the rail.

317
00:08:21,390 --> 00:08:22,930
I hadn't decided to.

318
00:08:22,930 --> 00:08:24,010
I just did it,

319
00:08:24,010 --> 00:08:27,010
then stopped halfway
down because I realized.

320
00:08:27,010 --> 00:08:27,960
By the end of the fourth

321
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:28,990
week I'd slept through

322
00:08:28,990 --> 00:08:30,910
the night four times running.

323
00:08:30,910 --> 00:08:32,010
I stood at the counter

324
00:08:32,010 --> 00:08:33,190
and finished making dinner

325
00:08:33,190 --> 00:08:34,910
without looking for the stool.

326
00:08:34,910 --> 00:08:36,620
None of that is dramatic.

327
00:08:36,620 --> 00:08:37,070
All of it

328
00:08:37,070 --> 00:08:39,080
was gone for two years.

329
00:08:39,080 --> 00:08:40,910
A few weeks
later my husband

330
00:08:40,910 --> 00:08:42,090
asked if I wanted to walk

331
00:08:42,090 --> 00:08:44,410
the long way
around the block.

332
00:08:44,410 --> 00:08:45,060
And for the first

333
00:08:45,060 --> 00:08:46,400
time in two years,

334
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:47,720
I said yes.

335
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:49,370
I wanted to understand why,

336
00:08:49,370 --> 00:08:51,530
so I read the whole thing.

337
00:08:51,530 --> 00:08:53,440
It comes down to four steps.

338
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:54,210
One.

339
00:08:54,210 --> 00:08:55,260
The tissue around a new

340
00:08:55,260 --> 00:08:56,510
knee can stay inflamed

341
00:08:56,510 --> 00:08:58,790
long after surgery is over.

342
00:08:59,180 --> 00:08:59,900
Two.

343
00:08:59,900 --> 00:09:02,100
Inflamed tissue
holds extra fluid,

344
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:02,730
so it takes up

345
00:09:02,730 --> 00:09:04,270
more room than it should.

346
00:09:04,270 --> 00:09:05,040
Three.

347
00:09:05,040 --> 00:09:06,940
There's only so
much room in there.

348
00:09:06,940 --> 00:09:08,460
Bending compresses it.

349
00:09:08,460 --> 00:09:10,470
Straightening pulls it tight.

350
00:09:10,790 --> 00:09:12,500
That's the squeeze.

351
00:09:12,500 --> 00:09:13,720
Four.

352
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,160
Red and near-infrared
light have

353
00:09:15,160 --> 00:09:17,550
been studied for calming
that inflammation,

354
00:09:17,550 --> 00:09:18,820
so the swelling
and the pressure

355
00:09:18,820 --> 00:09:20,240
can come down with it.

356
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:21,820
In a randomized trial,

357
00:09:21,820 --> 00:09:23,580
patients given
light therapy after

358
00:09:23,580 --> 00:09:25,750
a knee replacement
had less pain,

359
00:09:25,750 --> 00:09:27,310
less swelling
and better early

360
00:09:27,310 --> 00:09:29,380
movement than
those who weren't.

361
00:09:29,710 --> 00:09:32,370
A 2025 review
said the same,

362
00:09:32,370 --> 00:09:33,020
and was clear

363
00:09:33,020 --> 00:09:34,750
the evidence is still limited.

364
00:09:34,750 --> 00:09:35,720
I probably sound like

365
00:09:35,720 --> 00:09:37,680
a broken record
to my family.

366
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:39,060
But after two years of doing

367
00:09:39,060 --> 00:09:41,480
everything I was told
and getting nowhere,

368
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:42,440
you have no idea what

369
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:44,280
it's like to sleep
through the night,

370
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:45,620
say yes to the walk,

371
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:46,990
and get my life back.

372
00:09:46,990 --> 00:09:48,730
So take it from me.

373
00:09:48,730 --> 00:09:50,080
Don't spend another year

374
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:51,730
waiting for it to settle.

375
00:09:52,190 --> 00:09:54,240
Don't spend two
hundred a session.

376
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:55,500
More than ten
thousand people

377
00:09:55,500 --> 00:09:56,550
with pain after a knee

378
00:09:56,550 --> 00:09:59,010
replacement have
already tried this.

379
00:09:59,010 --> 00:10:00,830
Some had it
worse than I did.

380
00:10:00,830 --> 00:10:02,060
You can get the KenRelief

381
00:10:02,060 --> 00:10:03,670
wrap from their website,

382
00:10:03,670 --> 00:10:04,640
with a discount link

383
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:06,580
and ninety days to try it.

384
00:10:06,580 --> 00:10:08,460
If it doesn't do
anything for you,

385
00:10:08,460 --> 00:10:09,730
you get your money back

386
00:10:09,730 --> 00:10:11,080
and you keep the wrap.

387
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:12,020
They only release

388
00:10:12,020 --> 00:10:13,680
so many at that price.

389
00:10:13,680 --> 00:10:15,010
If it's still there,

390
00:10:15,010 --> 00:10:17,333
get one, and stop
the squeeze.
